From: alioth bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] alioth: opt-in power/reset and bounded SPI chip identification

Keep alitouch=1 as the existing stage-A probe. alitouch=2 additionally
validates idle SPI firmware/FIFO geometry and an inherited XO clock,
asserts GPIO33 reset, votes exact DT rails (ldoc1 1.8V then ldoc10 3.0V),
configures qup4 pins/mode0/8-bit FIFO, and reads FT IDs A3/9F with CRC.
The alioth RPMh entry point uses its DT reserved command DB, validates both
resource names before requesting power, and retains TCS timeout quarantine.
Sweet retains its original ldoc11 interface and DB locator.

No IC register writes, firmware upgrade, DMA, interrupts or HID events.
Transport faults stop further transfers; CRC/status retries are capped at3.
Full kernel build and physical ID5652 confirmation are still required.

